      "location": {
        "zh": "福建省泉州市鲤城区",
        "en": "Licheng District, Quanzhou, Fujian, China"
      },
      "type": {
        "zh": "建筑改造",
        "en": "Adaptive reuse"
      },
      "role": {
        "zh": "团队合作",
        "en": "Team project"
      },
      "description": {
        "zh": "项目以“半城烟火一页仙”为主题，回应泉州古城日常生活与精神性并存的气质。设计延续原建筑由礼拜堂、影院至仓库的历史记忆，以对称的板梁秩序与非对称的功能布局，组织中央通高书厅、书阶、书廊及咖啡厅，形成贯通多层的回游阅读路径。前院通过双入口区分游客与居民流线，后院以廊亭、台阶座椅衔接公共活动与街巷生活。天窗引入自然光，红铜色金属、清水混凝土与闽南“出砖入石”细节呼应地方材料与剧场记忆，让阅读、交流和日常停留在新旧空间之间自然发生。",
        "en": "Under the theme “Half a City of Everyday Life, a Page of Transcendence,” the project responds to the coexistence of everyday life and spiritual experience in historic Quanzhou. Retaining the building’s layered history as a chapel, cinema, and warehouse, the design combines a symmetrical beam-and-slab order with an asymmetrical arrangement of uses. A double-height book hall, stepped reading area, upper gallery, and café form a looping route across multiple levels. Two entrances distinguish visitor and resident circulation, while courtyard pavilions and stepped seating connect public activities with surrounding lanes. Skylights, copper-toned metal, exposed concrete, and local brick-and-stone details bring together reading, conversation, and everyday encounters within the old building."
      },
      "documents": [],
      "dateEnd": "2026-11",
      "period": {
        "zh": "2026年9月—11月",
        "en": "September–November 2026"
      }
